{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 100)` priors for the bounded scale parameters `sigma_a1`, `sigma_a2`, and `sigma_y`. These parameters already had finite Stan constraints `<lower=0, upper=100>`, so the added uniform statements are constant on the existing support and preserve the posterior up to a normalizing constant while satisfying SafeStan's requirement that every parameter have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before use. No data changes were made; `N`, `county`, `u`, and `x` remain context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=85> county;
  vector[N] u;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
transformed data {
  vector[N] inter;

  inter = u .* x;
}
parameters {
  vector[2] beta;
  vector[85] eta1;
  vector[85] eta2;
  real mu_a1;
  real mu_a2;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a1;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a2;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[85] a1;
  vector[85] a2;
  vector[N] y_hat;

  a1 = mu_a1 + sigma_a1 * eta1;
  a2 = 0.1 * mu_a2 + sigma_a2 * eta2;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a1[county[i]] + x[i] * a2[county[i]] + beta[1] * u[i]
               + beta[2] * inter[i];
  }
}
model {
  beta ~ normal(0, 100);

  mu_a1 ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_a2 ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta1 ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta2 ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a1 ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_a2 ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);

  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"county":[1,1,1],"u":[3.095263830103437,3.240803823622999,2.134870852219283],"x":[5.0791611210885055,2.7963246401033395,2.90628749790133],"y":[3.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
